    "title": "Pennsylvania State Police helicopter violently collides with plane, pilot dead: FAA - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kaylee Lindenmuth ,\n1 hours ago\nCARLISLE, Pa. ( WHTM ) -- An airplane and Pennsylvania State Police helicopter collided violently at the Carlisle Airport located in South Middleton Township, Pennsylvania, Wednesday evening, federal authorities confirmed to Nexstar's WHTM.\nTwo people were aboard the PSP aircraft when it collided midair with a Cessna 150 around 6:50 p.m., a Federal Aviation Administration spokesperson said in a statement. The plane was descending onto the runway and veered into the helicopter, according Lt. Col. George Bivens, Pennsylvania's acting state police commissioner.\n“When I say it was a very violent crash, that plane was cut into a lot of pieces,” Bivens said Wednesday night.\nGov. Josh Shapiro, who rushed to the incident, issued a statement, saying, in part: \"Lori and I are praying hard and we ask all of our fellow Pennsylvanians to join us.\"\nPhoto Courtesy / Jamie Luster Photo Courtesy / Jamie Luster Photo Courtesy / Brandi Freet The NTSB will lead an investigation along with the FAA,the agency confirmed to WHTM News.\nThe runway remains closed to fixed wing aircraft, according to an FAA Notice to Air Missions.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
    "summary": "CARLISLE, Pa. ( WHTM ) -- An airplane and Pennsylvania State Police helicopter collided violently at the Carlisle Airport located in South Middleton Township, Pennsylvania, Wednesday evening, federal authorities confirmed to Nexstar's WHTM. Two people were aboard the PSP aircraft when it collided midair with a Cessna 150 around 6:50 p.m., a Federal Aviation Administration spokesperson said in a statement. The plane was descending onto the runway and veered into the helicopter, according Lt. Col. George Bivens, Pennsylvania's acting state police commissioner.",
